@startuml
title TASK-260712-2lrpc0 - frozen capture, picker, and recovery flows

skinparam shadowing false
actor User
participant "Capture UI" as UI
participant "Cue sequencer" as Seq
participant "Capture writer" as Writer
database "Private media store" as Store
participant "Upload client" as Upload

== Record without cue contamination ==
User -> UI: Start
UI -> Writer: open (commit disabled)
UI -> Seq: begin
Seq --> UI: play start cue
UI -> Seq: start cue completed
Seq --> Writer: enable microphone commit
User -> UI: Stop
UI -> Seq: stop requested
Seq --> Writer: disable commit and close
Writer -> Store: fsync + validate + atomic rename
Store --> UI: self_test_local or durable_unsent
UI -> Seq: capture closed
Seq --> UI: play stop cue

alt self-test
  UI -> Store: close/delete
  Store --> UI: deleted; never uploadable
else user recording
  UI -> Upload: upload durable_unsent
  alt failure or outage
    Upload --> UI: unavailable
    note right of Store
    Durable draft remains for retry or explicit delete.
    end note
  else confirmed
    Upload --> UI: confirmed
    UI -> Store: cleanup
  end
end

== Picker intake ==
User -> UI: approve external file
UI -> UI: acquire scoped access
UI -> Store: copy bytes into opaque partial
UI -> UI: close external access
Store -> Store: validate + fsync + atomic rename
Store --> UI: durable_unsent

== Startup recovery ==
UI -> Store: recover
Store -> Store: delete all partials and self-tests
Store -> Store: delete invalid/truncated drafts
Store --> UI: retain valid durable_unsent drafts

note bottom
Real microphone, audible cue, restart, and hardware behavior are manual-epic evidence.
Automated evidence covers exact bytes, state parity, filesystem outcomes, and packaging.
end note

@enduml
